The standard specifies four nominal internal diameter bore sizes to match different flow networks:
a) 50 mm (Tolerance: +1.5 mm, -0 mm);
b) 63 mm (Tolerance: +1.5 mm, -0 mm);
c) 75 mm (Tolerance: +1.5 mm, -0 mm);
d) 90 mm (Tolerance: +1.5 mm, -0 mm).

Lay flat tubes are classified into two pressure types and must satisfy minimum burst pressures:
a) Nominal Bore 50 mm: Type I = 6.0 kg/cm², Type II = 8.0 kg/cm²;
b) Nominal Bore 63 mm: Type I = 6.0 kg/cm², Type II = 8.0 kg/cm²;
c) Nominal Bore 75 mm: Type I = 5.5 kg/cm², Type II = 7.0 kg/cm²;
d) Nominal Bore 90 mm: Type I = 5.0 kg/cm², Type II = 6.0 kg/cm².

Non-destructive (visual/dimensional) and destructive testing are performed on drawn samples:
- Up to 280: Non-destructive = 13 (Acceptance No = 1), Destructive = 8 (Acceptance No = 0);
- 281 to 500: Non-destructive = 20 (Acceptance No = 2), Destructive = 8 (Acceptance No = 0);
- 501 to 1 200: Non-destructive = 32 (Acceptance No = 3), Destructive = 13 (Acceptance No = 0);
- 1 201 to 3 200: Non-destructive = 50 (Acceptance No = 5), Destructive = 13 (Acceptance No = 0);
- 3 201 and above: Non-destructive = 80 (Acceptance No = 7), Destructive = 20 (Acceptance No = 1).

Under Amendment No. 2, each pack must be legibly and indelibly marked with standard batch details, manufacturer info, sizes, and the newly mandated items:
a) 'n) The information whether the material of the product is biocompatible that is, meets the requirement of the standard for biocompatibility evaluation – cytotoxicity, irritation and skin sensitization (if applicable)';
b) 'p) The word "MEDICAL USE"'.

Lots are grouped by identical construction and types. Random samples are selected for visual/dimensional and performance testing:
- Up to 50 rolls: Sample size = 3, Permissible defective rolls = 0;
- 51 to 150 rolls: Sample size = 5, Permissible defective rolls = 0;
- 151 to 300 rolls: Sample size = 8, Permissible defective rolls = 1 (Acceptance No. = 1, Rejection No. = 3);
- 301 to 500 rolls: Sample size = 13, Permissible defective rolls = 2;
- 501 rolls and above: Sample size = 20, Permissible defective rolls = 3.

The covers are classified into standard varieties based on reinforcement types:
a) Type I: Standard transparent covers without a laminated reinforcement band;
b) Type II: High-strength covers strategically fortified with a laminated reinforcement band at the edges and center to sustain high mechanical stresses under hailstorms.

Consignment lots are grouped by identical materials, shapes, and sizes under similar conditions of manufacture. Random samples must be drawn per Table 3 for non-destructive and destructive testing:
- Up to 280: Non-destructive = 13 (Acceptance No. = 1), Destructive = 5 (Acceptance No. = 0);
- 501 to 1 200: Non-destructive = 20 (Acceptance No. = 1), Destructive = 5 (Acceptance No. = 0);
- 10 001 to 35 000: Non-destructive = 50 (Acceptance No. = 3), Destructive = 8 (Acceptance No. = 0);
- 500 001 and over: Non-destructive = 125 (Acceptance No. = 7), Destructive = 13 (Acceptance No. = 0).
